{{!-- The Pub/Sub service account an API-based Gmail app uses to arm watches, shared by the
interactive `gmail` block and the `gmailService` one: both reach Gmail over the HTTP API, so both want
the same control, and the server-side `pubSubApp` field was never provider-specific.

`data-base-scopes="api"` is what reveals it - see checkScopesRadio() at the bottom of oauth_form.hbs. --}}

<div class="card-footer border-base-content/10 border-t px-6 py-4{{#unless baseScopesApi}} hidden{{/unless}}"
    data-base-scopes="api">

    <p class="mb-2">
        For faster webhook notifications, select a Gmail service account with the Pub/Sub Admin role.
        EmailEngine uses it to set up Google Cloud Pub/Sub for accounts managed by this app.
    </p>

    <p class="mb-2">
        <strong>Note:</strong> This is optional but recommended. With a Pub/Sub service account, EmailEngine
        receives changes in near real time. Without one, it falls back to polling each account about every 10
        minutes, so webhooks for new, updated, or deleted emails (and bounce detection) still fire, just with up
        to a 10-minute delay. Send-only accounts don't require this.
    </p>

    <label class="label-text" for="pubSubApp">Select service account to manage webhooks (optional). The service
        account must be for the same Google Cloud Project.</label>
    <select class="select w-full{{#if errors.pubSubApp}} is-invalid{{/if}}" id="pubSubApp"
        name="pubSubApp" {{#unless baseScopesApi}}disabled{{/unless}}>

        <option value="">Select the service account for your project</option>

        {{!-- Nothing disables an option here: the select carries that for the whole control, and
        filterPubSubApps() in oauth_form.hbs owns the per-option state so the two cannot fight. An
        {{#unless baseScopesApi}} inside this {{#each}} resolved against the ITEM rather than the page,
        so it shipped `disabled` on every option in every mode. --}}
        {{#each pubSubApps}}
        <option value="{{id}}" data-project="{{googleProjectId}}" {{#if selected}}selected{{/if}}>{{name}}{{#if
            description}} -
            {{description}}{{/if}} [{{googleProjectId}}]</option>
        {{/each}}

    </select>
    {{#if errors.pubSubApp}}
    <span class="helper-text text-error">{{errors.pubSubApp}}</span>
    {{/if}}
</div>
